{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/fields/satellites/","source":"students/subjects/physics/fields/satellites.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Satellites & Rockets | Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/fields/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to Fields</a></nav>\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-2\">Satellites &amp; Rockets</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Basic orbital mechanics and conceptual rocket equation ideas (qualitative).</p>\n\n      <h3 class=\"mt-6 text-md font-semibold\">Practice question</h3>\n      <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside text-gray-700\">\n        <li>Explain qualitatively why rockets require multiple stages to reach orbit.</li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <h3 class=\"mt-4 text-md font-semibold\">Brief solution</h3>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Staging discards empty fuel tanks and engines to reduce mass, improving mass ratio and allowing higher final speeds for a given fuel.</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif} .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(16px);backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}